355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (Carianne Fisher, NCCADV Executive Director, joined the staff at NCCADV in November 2019. She began her social work career as a weekend advocate at a domestic violence shelter in St. Louis. Carianne later joined the team at a private child welfare agency in Illinois for over 16 years. She began as a Family Counselor in a program serving youth who ran away from home in Southern Illinois. She later served as Training Coordinator, Director of Professional Education and Training, and Director of Human Resources and Training. Carianne was also the Human Resources Manager for a skilled nursing facility, a Field Consultant for the University of Chicago, and the Director of Training at Cook County Juvenile Temporary Detention Center. Before joining NCCADV, Carianne served as the first Executive Director of Therapet, an animal-assisted therapy nonprofit in Tyler, TX. Carianne received both a B.A. in English Literature and an MSW from Washington University in St Louis. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
