/P 176 0 R
/E (Shequana Pulliam serves as the Prevention Specialist for Domestic Violence Shelter and Services, Inc. \(DVSS\) in Wilmington, North Carolina. In this role, she collaborates with the North Carolina Coalition Against Domestic Violence \(NCCADV\) and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention \(CDC\) to strengthen trauma-informed support systems for local direct service providers. Her work focuses on promoting economic stability, supporting agency policies through partnerships with local businesses, and fostering positive community norms by creating opportunities for teens to engage in meaningful conversations with their peers about issues that matter to them. In January 2024, Shequana initiated the development of a Violence Prevention Coordinated Community Response Team \(CCRT\) to bridge service gaps and strengthen collaboration among community partners. Through this initiative, she works to address the intersection of shared risk and protective factors across agencies, creating a more coordinated and comprehensive approach to violence prevention throughout the community. Shequana is the mother of two beautiful young women and a member of Delta Sigma Theta Sorority, Incorporated. She also received her Community Resilience Model \(CRM\)Teaching Certification in August of 2025. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [5]
>>
