/Title (Richard Abiona is a communications professional and visual storyteller with a growing interest in technology and innovation, working at the intersection of media, advocacy, and emerging tech. His work focuses on amplifying the voices of underserved communities and supporting advocacy through compelling visual and written narratives. Before moving to the United States, Richard spent several years working with nonprofit organizations in Nigeria on initiatives addressing gender-based violence, police accountability, and COVID-19 relief for vulnerable communities. He holds a master's degree in Communication from North Carolina State University and is currently pursuing a master's degree in Technology Management at North Carolina A&T State University, where he serves as a Graduate Teaching Assistant. Most recently, he directed and edited Lights Still On, a documentary exploring the impact of funding cuts on domestic violence services, produced for the North Carolina Coalition Against Domestic Violence. Through his work, Richard seeks to tell stories that inform, inspire, and drive meaningful change.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 767 0 R
>>
